    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, my client has been stuck on their squat for like 3 weeks now. they can't seem to add any weight to the bar even though they're eating enough. how do deload weeks and changing up the volume actually help break a plateau like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Deload weeks reduce accumulated fatigue, allowing your nervous system and tendons to recover fully so you can return to training with perfect form and explosive strength. Changing volume breaks plateaus by shifting the glycogen demand and mechanical stress away from routine patterns your body has already adapted to, preventing adaptation stagnation. This strategic management of load ensures you are strong enough to handle heavier weights once progress stalls.",
